tps://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:23:41-07:00","id":1380737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380648-v5-corebook-pdf-on-sale-on-drivethrurpg?p=1380667#post1380667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone tell me if this PDF version contains the errata, like Lingering Kiss becoming an ally-buffing power or Prowess now adding half your dots in Potence to Melee weapon damage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think so. The most recent PDF copy (updated 8/2019) from Modiphius directly contains the Prowess and Lingering Kiss errata as well as the errata rewording Feral Weapons, so this PDF copy should contain it as well, since Modiphius would have supplied the file to DTRPG for distribution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T15:34:51-07:00","id":1380780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380648-v5-corebook-pdf-on-sale-on-drivethrurpg?p=1380737#post1380737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think so. The most recent PDF copy (updated 8/2019) from Modiphius directly contains the Prowess and Lingering Kiss errata as well as the errata rewording Feral Weapons, so this PDF copy should contain it as well, since Modiphius would have supplied the file to DTRPG for distribution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended up buying it and it indeed does, which is nice to see. Although I'm disappointed that Lingering Kiss was re-errataed to boost only Social pools rather than a category of the drinker's choice. Although - what exactly defines the category of pool? Is it the attribute, or the skill, or what? Would Strength + Intimidation be a Social pool? Composure + Firearms? Wits + Insight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T19:37:22-07:00","id":1380830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380648-v5-corebook-pdf-on-sale-on-drivethrurpg?p=1380780#post1380780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ended up buying it and it indeed does, which is nice to see. Although I'm disappointed that Lingering Kiss was re-errataed to boost only Social pools rather than a category of the drinker's choice. Although - what exactly defines the category of pool? Is it the attribute, or the skill, or what? Would Strength + Intimidation be a Social pool? Composure + Firearms? Wits + Insight?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not 100% defined, so a lot of it is Storyteller discretion. Personally I look at what the outcome is actually going to be, or the actual narrative use of the pool, to determine, along with what Attribute and/or Skill categories are used. Like, just with a CTRL+F through the book a couple of times it mentions Social dice pools it mentions the obvious Social skills. So something like Str + melee is obviously physical, or intelligence + occult is obviously Mental. But something more odd, like Strength + Intimidation, would be social (to me) because it's looking for a social response, not a physical response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:36:27-07:00","id":1381402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380648-v5-corebook-pdf-on-sale-on-drivethrurpg?p=1380830#post1380830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's not 100% defined, so a lot of it is Storyteller discretion. Personally I look at what the outcome is actually going to be, or the actual narrative use of the pool, to determine, along with what Attribute and/or Skill categories are used. Like, just with a CTRL+F through the book a couple of times it mentions Social dice pools it mentions the obvious Social skills. So something like Str + melee is obviously physical, or intelligence + occult is obviously Mental. But something more odd, like Strength + Intimidation, would be social (to me) because it's looking for a social response, not a physical response.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games, anything that is using a social attribute, OR a social skill, Still falls in the category of social dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26038-feargrounds","name":"FearGrounds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}